              "id": "SC-2-LogViewerView-onActivity",
              "metric": "SC-2",
              "severity": "SEVERE",
              "description": "Unstructured Task at line 422 is created inside the bridge.onActivity escaping closure (set from inside the .task modifier, but invoked by the bridge whenever activity fires — outside the .task scope). The Task has no stored handle and no .cancel() path, so each activity callback spawns a fire-and-forget Task that survives view dismissal. This is the SC-2 'orphaned task' pattern: store the handle on the view-model and cancel in deinit/onDisappear, or have the bridge expose an AsyncSequence that the .task modifier consumes (so cancellation is structured).",
